## Change summary

On the base `/train.php` page, the selected-league benchmark feature now uses the approved single-card workspace:

- league IDs, links, calculation control, status, and VPS cache state are placed in the left control pane;
- the existing role benchmark results and profile actions are placed in the right results pane;
- the native top-player skill-average block is suppressed on this page;
- responsive layout stacks controls above results without page-level horizontal overflow.

## Approved scope

- Repository mutation: yes
- Canonical approval phrase: `commit approved`
- Approved changed files:
  - `src/modules/team-management/training-reference-guide.js`
  - `tests/browser/test_fm2026_design_adapter.py`
- Out of scope:
  - benchmark formulas and aggregation;
  - VPS/API/cache schema;
  - league IDs and destination links;
  - profile application behavior;
  - player training tables;
  - other routes;
  - generated release artifacts.

## Verification

The browser regression verifies:

- one workspace with the control pane first and results pane second;
- five league controls and eight role-result rows loaded from a VPS-shaped fixture;
- desktop side-by-side geometry;
- responsive stacked geometry;
- native top-player averages remain in the DOM but are hidden and inaccessible;
- repeated mounts do not duplicate the workspace;
- content containment and horizontal-overflow boundaries remain valid.

Local syntax checks completed for the changed JavaScript and Python files. Post-write blob hashes match the complete branch files.

